# {{ .ProviderName }}

A Crossplane provider for managing `{{ .TerraformProvider }}` resources,
generated from its Terraform provider schema via
[upjet](https://github.com/crossplane/upjet).

## Getting Started

### Install Provider

Apply a `Provider` package pointing at your built (and pushed) image:

```yaml
apiVersion: pkg.crossplane.io/v1
kind: Provider
metadata:
  name: {{ .ProviderName }}
spec:
  package: {{ .Repo }}:latest
```

For local development without pushing anywhere, use `make local-deploy` instead
(see Development below) — it builds the image, spins up a kind cluster, and
deploys it in one step.

### Configure Provider

Apply a ProviderConfig and its credentials Secret:

```bash
kubectl apply -f examples/providerconfig/providerconfig.yaml
```

## Development

### Build

```bash
make generate   # fetch the Terraform schema, generate types and controllers
make build      # build the provider binary and the deployable image
```

### Test

```bash
make test           # unit tests
make local-deploy   # kind cluster + Crossplane + this provider
make e2e             # + uptest against examples/*/*.yaml
```
